Observation
Row 1 → 1 number
Row 2 → 2 numbers
Row 3 → 3 numbers
Row 4 → 4 numbers
Numbers are consecutive.

Logic
Maintain a variable num / count = 1.
Outer loop runs from 1 to N (rows).
Inner loop runs from 1 to row number.
Print num and increment it.

DRY RUN-->
i controls the rows.
j controls how many numbers are printed in each row.
count stores the current consecutive number.
After printing a number, count++ increases it for the next position.


import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);  //The Scanner is used to take input from the user.
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        int count = 1;
        
        for(int i =1; i<=n; i++){
            for(int j =1;j<=i;j++){
                
                System.out.println(count++ + "\t");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
        sc.close();
    }
}


